[
    {
        "content": "<p>Given a subgroup H of a group G and (g : G), how to express the subgroup gHg^-1 ? As much as I can shorten, it should be <code>H.map (MulAut.conj g).toMonoidHom</code> or <code>(H.map (MulAut.conj g) : Subgroup G)</code>. Did I miss something on Mathlib? I couldn't find something like <code>Subgroup.conj</code>. There is only <code>Subgroup.Normal.conjAct</code>where H is assumed to be normal. In Sylow's second theorem, <code>IsPretransitive G (Sylow p G)</code> is used to express that all Sylow p-groups are conjugate, but this is not the notion I need. I supposed there should be something like Subgroup.conj : G \\-&gt; Subgroup G \\-&gt; Subgroup G so that I could use <code>Subgroup.conj g H.</code>Could someone point out the correct doc#? Thanks!</p>",
        "id": 606378153,
        "sender_full_name": "Jiaxi Mo",
        "timestamp": 1782350239
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"644391\">@loogle</span> \"conj\", Subgroup, |- (_ : Type _)</p>",
        "id": 606380426,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1782352328
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"search\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f50d\" role=\"img\" title=\"search\">:search:</span> <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/GroupTheory/GroupAction/ConjAct.html#ConjAct.Subgroup.conjAction\">ConjAct.Subgroup.conjAction</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/GroupTheory/GroupAction/ConjAct.html#ConjAct.Subgroup.conjMulDistribMulAction\">ConjAct.Subgroup.conjMulDistribMulAction</a>, and <a href=\"https://loogle.lean-lang.org/?q=%22conj%22%2C%20Subgroup%2C%20%7C-%20%28_%20%3A%20Type%20_%29\">6 more</a></p>",
        "id": 606380428,
        "sender_full_name": "loogle",
        "timestamp": 1782352330
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"816344\">@Aaron Liu</span> loogle's relevant results are ones with H being normal. It does not make sense that Mathlib added the normal case but not the general case. I guess it is hidden somewhere in Mathlib?</p>",
        "id": 606393853,
        "sender_full_name": "Jiaxi Mo",
        "timestamp": 1782361574
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Does this make sense?:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Group</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subgroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ConjAct</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">scoped</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Pointwise</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 606400763,
        "sender_full_name": "Bryan Wang",
        "timestamp": 1782366255
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"934803\">@Bryan Wang</span> Thanks a lot! You are right. It does:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">subgroup_conj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">MulAut</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">conj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toMonoidHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subgroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I thought at first that <code>g • H</code> means the coset gH and didn't notice that (g  : ConjAct G), since it does present the coset somewhere. Sorry, I should have been able to figure this out myself instead of asking on Zulip. But how can I navigate myself to this kind of notions next time, so that I don't need to post such naive questions here? Or could you please give me some hint about the general design<code>\\smul</code> or <code>ConjAct</code> that I am missing? I am confused now how does Lean know <code>\\smul</code> should return a subgroup here...</p>",
        "id": 606405511,
        "sender_full_name": "Jiaxi Mo",
        "timestamp": 1782368700
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"1097608\">Jiaxi Mo</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Conjugate.20of.20subgroups/near/606405511\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Sorry, I should have been able to figure this out myself instead of asking on Zulip. </p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>No no, I think this is exactly the sort of thing that one can only figure out by asking on zulip at this point in time! I myself figured these things out by zulip and getting more experience with mathlib (and a lot of searching in the <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/\">mathlib docs</a>) <span aria-label=\"sweat smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f605\" role=\"img\" title=\"sweat smile\">:sweat_smile:</span></p>\n<p>I believe the <a href=\"#narrow/channel/579630-Project-announcements/topic/The.20Mathlib.20phrasebook/with/600032051\">mathlib phrasebook</a> is meant to help with such things in the long term!</p>\n<p>edit: Indeed, looking at the phrasebook now, sections 6.2 and 6.3 cover this!</p>",
        "id": 606418013,
        "sender_full_name": "Bryan Wang",
        "timestamp": 1782373541
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Personally I would usually use <code>MulAut.conj g • H</code> over the type synonym <code>ConjAct</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Group</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subgroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">scoped</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Pointwise</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MulAut</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">conj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 606419802,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Browning",
        "timestamp": 1782374072
    },
